+# Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope, Filtering the Directory by a Shown Attribute Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable records. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so whether it was deliberate stayed unknown.
+
+A request on 2026-11-05 asked to filter the veterinarian directory by specialty. Read against the row as written, that filter is a way of finding veterinarians, and the request alone cannot reopen a recorded non-goal. The owner decided the row at intake.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole.** Decline the filter. Rejected by the owner.
+2. **Drop NG-9 for veterinarians.** Open every form of veterinarian search. Rejected: free-text search would repeat what owner search already demonstrates.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text veterinarian search stays out; filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in.
+
+## Decision
+
+The owner's decision, quoted from the intake record: "Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in."
+
+Searching for a pet or a visit stays out of scope, unchanged. Specialty is the attribute the directory already shows, so a specialty filter falls inside the narrowed boundary.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The directory may be filtered by specialty. The first such capability is `REQ-VET-003`.
+- Free-text search for a veterinarian by name, or by any text the directory does not show as an attribute, remains declined.
+- A filter on a further shown attribute needs no new non-goal decision, but needs its own requirement.
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation for its veterinarian clause. Its pet and visit clauses remain part of it.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the first capability inside the narrowed boundary.
