+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty name, when the directory is opened with it, then only veterinarians holding that specialty are listed, a page at a time over the narrowed list.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty name, when the machine-readable list is requested with it, then only veterinarians holding that specialty are returned.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty name differing from a held specialty only by letter case, when either form is requested with it, then it matches.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given only the start of a specialty name, when either form is requested with it, then no veterinarian matches.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when either form is requested with it, then the usual page or list is returned with no veterinarians and no failure.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given an empty or space-only specialty, when either form is requested with it, then the result equals the result with no specialty.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a narrowed directory spanning several pages, when the reader moves between pages, then every page stays narrowed to the same specialty.
 
