+## Scale and Load
+
+Veterinarian data is small and read-mostly, and every path below is treated as bounded. Unfiltered vet-list reads are shared and cached in the vet cache. Specialty-filtered reads are request-private and uncached; caller-chosen values never enter the cache.
+
+| Data set or path | Realistic size | Growth | Access pattern | Form |
+|------------------|----------------|--------|----------------|------|
+| Veterinarians and their specialties | Six veterinarians and three specialties in the seed data; production size unrecorded, treated as bounded | No write path in the application | Shared read-mostly | Specialties load eagerly with each veterinarian |
+| Unfiltered vet list, HTML and machine-readable | Bounded by the veterinarians row | — | Shared read-mostly | One query per page, or one for the whole list; results cached in the vet cache |
+| Specialty-filtered vet list, HTML and machine-readable | Bounded by the veterinarians row | — | Request-private | One database query: whole-name equality on the specialty, compared in a single letter case, distinct veterinarians. Paged on the HTML route, whole list on the machine-readable route. Not cached |
+
+- **Hot paths:** none recorded.
+- **Limits:** unrecorded. The vet cache declares no size limit; only unfiltered reads populate it.
+
 ## Dependency Policy
 
 Minimize external dependencies. Every dependency is an attack surface and a maintenance burden.
